    <IRS990ScheduleO documentId="RetDoc5">
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990 - ORGANIZATION'S MISSION</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>TO ORGANIZE ALL UNORGANIZED PROFESSIONAL, TECHNICAL, OFFICE AND CLERICAL EMPLOYEES, TO SECURE TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT FOR ITS MEMBERS CONSISTENT WITH IDEAS OF FAIR WAGES AND BENEFITS TO PROMOTE AND ENCOURAGE HARMONIOUS RELATIONS BETWEEN OURSELVES AND OUR EMPLOYERS TO RENDER ALL POSSIBLE ASSISTANCE TO OUR FELLOW MEMBERS IN THE AMERICAN FEDERATION OF LABOR AND CONGRESS OF INDUSTRIAL ORGANIZATIONS (AFL-CIO) AND TO HAVE, IN GENERAL, THE SAME AIMS AND PURPOSES AS THE INTERNATIONAL UNION (INTERNATIONAL UNION OR OPEIU) PROVIDES FOR ITS CONSTITUTION IN THE INTEREST OF ALL PROFESSIONAL, TECHNICAL, OFFICE AND CLERICAL EMPLOYEES.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PAGE 2, PART III, LINE 4D</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>TO PROMOTE AND FOSTER GOODWILL AND PUBLIC SUPPORT FOR THE WELFARE AND INTEREST OF THIS UNION AND ITS MEMBERS BY ACTIONS INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO: ORGANIZING THE UNORGANIZED, SPONSORING ACTIVITIES THAT CONSERVE THE INTERESTS OF THIS UNION AND SERVE ITS MEMBERSHIP, AND PROVIDING DONATIONS TO SUPPORT LABOR FRIENDLY ORGANIZATIONS AND OTHER ORGANIZATIONS IN OUR LOCAL COMMUNITY.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PAGE 6, PART VI, LINE 6</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE LOCAL IS A MEMBERSHIP ORGANIZATION. MEMBERS ARE MADE UP OF EMPLOYEES REPRESENTED UNDER A COLLECTIVE BARGAINING AGREEMENT. MEMBERSHIP IS MADE UP OF THE FOLLOWING CLASSES: REGULAR MEMBERS: ARE FULL TIME EMPLOYEES WITHIN THE BARGAINING UNIT, HAVE FULL VOTING RIGHTS, AND PAY THE FULL MEMBERSHIP FEE. RETIRED MEMBERS: HAVE VOTING RIGHTS AND PAY A REDUCED FLAT RATE OF 5. ON-CALL EMPLOYEES AND/OR MEMBERS: ARE TEMPORARY EMPLOYEES WHO ARE ON-CALL BY THEIR EMPLOYER, KAISER. THESE EMPLOYEES AND/OR MEMBERS DO NOT PAY DUES AND THEIR FEES VARY ACCORDING TO THEIR HOURS WORKED. SINCE THEY DO NOT PAY THE FULL MEMBERSHIP DUES AND INITIATION FEES, THEY DO NOT HAVE VOTING RIGHTS. WORK PERMIT MEMBERS: ARE NEW HIRES WHO PAY THE PERMIT FEE PER MONTH, WHICH IS THE SAME AMOUNT AS THE REGULAR MEMBERSHIP DUES FEE. THESE MEMBERS DO NOT PAY THE INITIATION FEE, THEREFORE, THEY DO NOT HAVE VOTING RIGHTS.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PAGE 6, PART VI, LINE 7A</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>REGULAR AND RETIRED MEMBERS IN GOOD STANDING (DUES ARE PAID CURRENT) ELECT THE MEMBERS OF THE GOVERNING BODY AS PRESCRIBED BY THE BYLAWS DURING ELECTION PERIOD EVERY THREE YEARS, AND AS VACANCIES BECOME AVAILABLE.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PAGE 6, PART VI, LINE 7B</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>REGULAR AND RETIRED MEMBERS IN GOODSTANDING (DUES ARE PAID CURRENT) VOTE ON SIGNIFICANT DECISIONS OF THE ORGANIZATION AS PRESCRIBED BY THE BYLAWS.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PAGE 6, PART VI, LINE 11B</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>FORM 990 WAS REVIEWED BY THE OFFICERS BEFORE THE FORM WAS SUBMITTED TO THE IRS.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PAGE 6, PART VI, LINE 12C</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE LOCAL PERIODICALLY UPDATES, MONITORS AND ENFORCES THE COMPLIANCE OF THE CONFLICT OF INTEREST, WHISTLEBLOWER POLICY, AND DOCUMENTATION RETENTION AND DESTRUCTION POLICIES IN A WRITTEN PREAMBLE.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PAGE 6, PART VI, LINE 15A</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>COMPENSATION IS APPROVED BY THE GOVERNING BOARD IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE CONSTITUTION AND BYLAWS AND THROUGH WRITTEN EMPLOYMENT CONTRACTS.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PAGE 6, PART VI, LINE 15B</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>COMPENSATION IS APPROVED BY THE GOVERNING BOARD IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE CONSTITUTION AND BYLAWS AND THROUGH WRITTEN EMPLOYMENT CONTRACTS.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PAGE 6, PART VI, LINE 19</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>FINANCIAL INFORMATION AND GOVERNING DOCUMENTATION ARE MADE PUBLICLY AVAILABLE ON THE FOMR LM-2, ELECTRONICALLY FILED WITH THE DEPARTMENT OF LABOR, ON THE DEPARTMENT OF LABOR PUBLIC DISCLOSURE WEBSITE. ANY OTHER REQUEST FOR FINANCIAL INFORMATION IS MADE AVAILABLE TO THE REQUESTOR UPON REQUEST.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART XI, LINE 9</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>RENTAL EXPENSES SHOWN IN EXPENSES ON FIN STMTS 154,709 INVESTMENT BROKER FEE SHOWN IN EXPENSES ON FIN STMTS -6,873 RENTAL EXPENSES REPORTED IN REVENUE ON 990 -154,709 INVESTMENTS BROKER FEE REPORTED IN REVENUE ON 990 6,873</ExplanationTxt>
